<Layout
	title="AmberTTY support — Peculiar Engineer"
	description="Requirements, common questions, and contact details for the AmberTTY SSH and AI Terminal app."
	kind="page"
	showDate={false}
>
	<h2>What you need</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>iPhone or iPad running iOS / iPadOS 18 or later</li>
		<li>An SSH server, dev machine, homelab box, or DigitalOcean / Cloudflare account</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Common questions</h2>

	<h3>Why do AI Agent sessions use <code>tmux</code>?</h3>
	<p>
		iOS and iPadOS suspend background network sockets shortly after you switch apps. Running
		Claude Code, Antigravity (<code>agy</code>), Codex, Aider, or OpenCode inside
		<code>tmux</code> keeps your agent alive on your server even if your phone sleeps or
		switches networks. When you return, AmberTTY reattaches to the running session with one tap.
	</p>

	<h3>Should I use a Secure Enclave key or an Ed25519 key?</h3>
	<p>
		<strong>Secure Enclave P-256</strong> keeps the private key inside your device hardware and
		never leaves the device. <strong>Ed25519</strong> supports optional per-key iCloud Keychain
		sync if you want the same key across iPhone and iPad.
	</p>

	<h3>What minimal API permissions do DigitalOcean &amp; Cloudflare need?</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>DigitalOcean token:</strong> <code>droplet:create</code>,
			<code>droplet:read</code>, <code>droplet:delete</code>, <code>ssh_key:create</code>,
			<code>ssh_key:read</code>.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Cloudflare token:</strong> <code>Zone:DNS:Edit</code> and
			<code>Account:Cloudflare Tunnel:Read</code>.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>API tokens are stored strictly in this device's Keychain and are never synced to iCloud.</p>

	<h3>Why does AmberTTY ask for Local Network permission?</h3>
	<p>
		iOS requires Local Network access to connect to SSH hosts on your LAN (such as
		<code>192.168.x.x</code> or <code>.local</code>). If you accidentally denied it, re-enable
		it in <strong>iOS Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Local Network → AmberTTY</strong>.
	</p>

	<h3>How do I restore AmberTTY Pro on another device?</h3>
	<p>
		Open <strong>Settings → AmberTTY Pro → Restore Purchases</strong> while signed into the same
		Apple Account used for your original purchase.
	</p>

